.TH XSETWALL 1 "September 2026" "xsetwall 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xsetwall - set an X11 wallpaper from an image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xsetwall
.RB [ -w | --white-border ]
.RB [ -s | --scale " scale" ]
.I image
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xsetwall
sets the desktop wallpaper using an image on an X11 display.

The image is scaled to fit the screen while preserving its aspect ratio.
The resulting image is centered on the screen.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -w ", " --white-border
Fill the unused area around the scaled image with white.

Without this option, the unused area is left black.

.TP
.BI -s " scale"
.BR --scale = scale
Set a custom image scale factor.

The scale must be a positive floating-point number.

For example, a scale of
.B 0.5
renders the image at half of its original dimensions.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B xsetwall wallpaper.jpg
Set
.B wallpaper.jpg
as the wallpaper using automatic scaling.

.TP
.B xsetwall -w wallpaper.png
Set the wallpaper and fill unused space with white.

.TP
.B xsetwall --white-border wallpaper.png
Equivalent to the previous example using the long option.

.TP
.B xsetwall -s 0.5 wallpaper.jpg
Scale the image to 50% of its original size.

.TP
.B xsetwall --scale 0.25 wallpaper.jpg
Scale the image to 25% of its original size.

.TP
.B xsetwall -w -s 0.75 wallpaper.png
Scale the image to 75% and fill unused space with white.

.SH NOTES
The program requires an X11 display.

Automatic scaling is calculated from the dimensions of the image and the screen.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.

.TP
.B 64
Invalid command-line usage.

.TP
.B 65
The input image contains invalid or inappropriate data.

.TP
.B 70
An internal software error occurred.

.TP
.B 71
An operating-system error occurred.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
Specifies the X11 display to use.

